id: pm-cf4t42
title: "GH-1186: unrecoverable legacy merge-receipt references block strict health with diagnostic-only remediation"
description: "A fleet upgrade to pm 2026.9.3 exposes durable history references to receipts that older releases stored only in ignored clone-local runtime directories. Strict health blocks on merge_receipt_history_reference_missing, merge reconcile reports no pending work, and the remediation map points back to health diagnostics. The receipt was never committed and cannot be recovered in another clone."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-03T18:06:41.043Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-03T18:07:09.388Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Legacy clone-local-only receipt references are identified without weakening current receipt validation; a supported audited disposition or version-aware advisory can settle genuinely unrecoverable references; every blocking remediation demonstrably progresses state; schema_or_identity_invalid names the failed identity check and reports stable evidence provenance; mixed-version fleet fixtures and strict-exit negative controls cover the upgrade path
parent: pm-dj98
risk: critical
confidence: high
severity: critical
environment: pm-cli 2026.9.3 upgrading repositories pinned between 2026.8.26 and 2026.8.31; Node 26.5.0; Linux
repro_steps: Open a repository whose historical merge_reconcile event references a receipt formerly written only under ignored runtime state; run pm merge reconcile --dry-run and then pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers.
expected_result: "Every strict-health blocking finding has an executable, auditable remediation or a version-aware advisory classification when the historical evidence is provably unrecoverable."
actual_result: "Reconcile reports clean and changes nothing while strict health exits 1 for a missing reference; remediation_map names the diagnostic itself, leaving no state-progressing path."
component: health/merge-receipts
